course: dictionary
lesson: 14500
title: A doctor for children
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A pediatrician is a doctor who looks after babies, children and teenagers. The word starts with «pedi», a part that is linked to children, and it ends with «-ician», which means a person who is an expert in something. Put them together and you get a children's doctor.
explain: «Mia took her baby brother to the pediatrician for his check-up.» A check-up is a visit to see if you are growing well and staying healthy. The words around the pediatrician tell you this is a doctor for babies and children, and the check-up clue shows what the doctor does.
explain: «My cousin sees a pediatrician because she has asthma.» Here the pediatrician helps with an illness. Try swapping in «children's doctor» and read the sentence again. If it still makes sense, your meaning is right.
fact: A pediatrician is a doctor who specially looks after babies, children and teenagers.
fact: A pediatrician checks how children grow, gives vaccinations and treats children's illnesses.
fact: In the USA, children often see a pediatrician for check-ups.
fact: In the UK, the spelling is «paediatrician». A family GP sees children first, and may send them to a paediatrician at the hospital if they need one.
exercise: «The pediatrician listened to the baby's heartbeat.» What is a pediatrician? | A teacher who works in a school | *A doctor for babies, children and teenagers | A nurse who cooks food in a hospital | A vet who looks after pets
exercise: «The pediatrician checked how fast Sam was growing.» What did the pediatrician check? | *How well Sam was growing | The football score | His favourite food | The colour of his bedroom
exercise: «Lily's pediatrician gave her a vaccination at the clinic.» Find and copy the word for the injection that protects you from illness. | Lily | clinic | *vaccination | pediatrician
test: Which is the UK spelling of this word? | pedeatrician | paedatrician | pediatritian | *paediatrician
test: Why might a child in the UK see a paediatrician at the hospital? | Because hospitals sell sweets there | Because the school asked them to | *Because the family GP sent them there for special care | Because they want to be a doctor when they grow up
exam: Which best describes a pediatrician? | *A doctor who looks after babies, children and teenagers | A teacher who teaches science | A nurse who works only in care homes | A doctor who checks teeth only
